 "tier1Summary": "Europe goes into its budget summit with one veto lifted and another threatened. Hungary let Ukraine's and Moldova's next accession clusters move forward, while [[p:António Costa]] trimmed the 2028–34 budget to win over frugal states. The Commission's €45bn Ukraine loan for 2027 needs all 27, and [[p:Robert Fico]] says Slovakia is out.\n\nAt home, France's budgets hit a 26 Nov deadline, Belgium's government has until Monday to agree a budget, Sweden still has no government, and Spain votes on 29 Nov with the right ahead. [[e:COP31|2026 United Nations Climate Change Conference]] is in overtime.\n\nElsewhere, a burning Russian military cargo ship drifted into Finnish waters after a drone strike, and Iran says it hit US bases in Bahrain.",
